 above, respectively, and then stirred in the dark for 24 h at 37 °C. The two phases were separated and determined by UV spectrophotometer, and the concentration in n-octanol (Co) and in PBS (Cw) was obtained ac-cording to the standard curves. The log P were obtained according the formula: log Po/w= log Co/Cw."}]}